    "narrative": {
      "care_continuity": [
        "The national isolation/CTE census is 751 patients, but it is not the sum of its published parts: the three provinces that publish a care block total 752 (Ituri 577, Nord-Kivu 170, Tshopo 5) and neither Haut-Uele, with 139 cumulative cases, nor Sud-Kivu publishes one at all.",
        "Ituri reports 577 patients against 991 beds (58.2% occupancy), split 235 confirmed and 342 suspects with 43 children under five; the aggregate conceals saturated units at Bambu and Mangala (confirmed and suspect), Nizi (confirmed), and Fataki, Kilo and Kigonze on the suspect side.",
        "Nord-Kivu reports 170 patients against 206 beds (82.5% occupancy) with 19 children under five; Tshopo holds 5 patients on 12 beds at the Kisangani centre.",
        "A new 60-bed building opened at the Mongbwalu treatment centre, the only capacity addition this edition records."
      ],
      "highlights": [
        "The DRC headline is 5021 confirmed cases and 2378 confirmed deaths; the country-scope endpoint is 5041 confirmed and 2380 deaths after the separately sourced Uganda 20/2 anchor.",
        "The edition records 76 new confirmed cases in 24 hours: 63 in Ituri, 11 in Nord-Kivu, 1 in Haut-Uele and 1 in Tshopo, with no new affected health zone; the footprint holds at 55 of 151.",
        "The front page reports 30 community deaths while the zone table prints 30 community plus 23 intra-CTE for the same 24 hours, so the day's confirmed-death total is 53 and the front-page figure is the community subset only.",
        "Contact follow-up falls to 82.2% (16130 of 19630) from 85.3% one edition earlier, and the edition twice describes that figure as meeting the 85% threshold it is in fact below.",
        "This is the first of three editions INSP released together on 20 August after four silent days, so the publication clock and the data clock separate by four days."
      ]
    },
