      "challenges": [
        "Weak alert escalation and incomplete listing and follow-up of contacts around confirmed cases.",
        "Points of entry remain under-operationalised in Tshopo: 7 of 20 sites active (35%) with 57.1% reporting completeness, for want of training, supervision, and logistic and financial support; in Ituri only 1 of 11 strategic sites runs without interruption.",
        "Responders unpaid in Ituri, Nord-Kivu and Haut-Uele, causing a strike that deprived six Haut-Uele points of entry of reporting entirely.",
        "2373 screening refusals recorded in Nord-Kivu (3.07%), and weak screening at the Pont-Shari post in Ituri for want of uniformed-service involvement; rumours about the origin of the disease persist among the stated reasons for refusal.",
        "Infection-prevention delivery short in Ituri: 21 of 97 expected rings opened and 48 of 97 sites decontaminated, attributed to insufficient teams and decontamination inputs (Mandima, Bambu-mine, Mangala), family resistance (Kilo), unfound addresses, insecurity and a decontaminators' strike; PCI reporting completeness limited to 9 of 14 Ituri health zones.",
        "Referral capacity short: 2 ambulances out of service in Ituri, only 6 available in Nord-Kivu, and 10 further ambulances needed in Haut-Uele.",
        "Treatment capacity saturated in Ituri (Bambu and Mangala confirmed and suspect, Nizi confirmed, Fataki, Kilo and Kigonze suspect); Tshopo has two incinerators out of service at the Makiso-Kisangani referral hospital and 309 kg of chlorine against a 1800 kg requirement."
