    "preserved_conflicts": [
      "24-hour death split: the front-page highlights state '76 newly confirmed cases including 30 (community) deaths', naming only the community component, while the edition's own zone table prints 30 community plus 23 intra-CTE deaths for the same 24 hours, totalling 53. The zone table is internally consistent and closes on every province, so 53 is promoted as the 24-hour confirmed-death figure and the front-page 30 is preserved as the community subset it actually describes. A reader taking the highlights at face value would understate the day's confirmed deaths by 43%.",
      "Contact follow-up threshold: the surveillance text states follow-up 'remonte a 82,2% ... au-dessus du seuil de 85%' and the key-messages box repeats that 82.2% 'atteint le seuil de 85,0%'. 82.2% is below 85%, in both places. The rate is promoted as printed and the edition's own reading of it against its threshold is preserved as wrong.",
      "Contact denominator scope: the printed national 16130/19630 excludes Bas-Uele. The four counted provinces sum exactly to those figures; adding the printed Bas-Uele row (35/185) gives 16165/19815, or 81.6%. The national figure is promoted as printed and the scope difference disclosed.",
      "Isolation census does not sum: the national headline prints 751 patients in isolation/CTE while the three provinces publishing a care block sum to 752 (Ituri 577, Nord-Kivu 170, Tshopo 5). Haut-Uele publishes no care block despite 139 cumulative cases, and neither does Sud-Kivu. The national figure is promoted as printed and the one-patient excess disclosed.",
      "Tshopo alert reporting status: the alert table's own footnote states Tshopo's data are unavailable for the period, while the same table prints a complete Tshopo row (48 alerts received, 2 validated, 2 investigated, 2 transferred). Each figure is carried where the edition prints it and the contradiction preserved.",
      "SitRep 94 is DRC-only at 5021 confirmed / 2378 deaths; the country-scope snapshot adds the stable Uganda 20/2/11 anchor separately -> 5041 / 2380 / 1072."
    ],
